============================================================================================================
PART 0 -- CONTROL: linear growth is LCDM-identical (L93); the boost is a NONLINEAR effect.
============================================================================================================
  [PASS] CTRL-1  at LINEAR order the cuscuton-MOND growth equation is LCDM's (c_s^2=0, G_eff=G, MOND cubic and dropped -- established in L93 to machine precision), so the CMB and the large-scale power spectrum are SAFE and the early-galaxy boost must be a NONLINEAR (collapse-regime) effect, not a linear one   (linear growth = LCDM (L93); boost enters only nonlinearly when g_N < a0)

